  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Ardeparin and Pulmonary Embolism (disease) through a series of indirect pathways. Ardeparin is associated with two indications, Purpura Fulminans and Disseminated Intravascular Coagulation, both of which are linked to Enoxaparin and Adomiparin, respectively. These latter entities are indicated to cause Pulmonary Embolism (disease). The scores for these pathways are consistent, indicating a moderate level of confidence in the proposed relationships. The mechanisms involve the involvement of coagulation pathways and inflammatory responses, which are commonly implicated in the development of Pulmonary Embolism. While the evidence is strong, it is important to note that the pathways are indirect and may not represent direct therapeutic or pathophysiological links. The integration of these pathways suggests that Ardeparin may be associated with an increased risk of Pulmonary Embolism through its role in triggering coagulation and inflammatory processes.",
